\documentclass{article}
\title{Succinct Arguments for Verifiable Computation}
\author{P. Nazari}
\date{January 2026}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\section{Setup}
A prover convinces a verifier that a delegated computation was carried out correctly.
We denote the transcript of the interaction by \tq and analyse how its length
grows with the security parameter of the underlying commitment scheme.
Verification runs in time polylogarithmic in the size of the circuit,
which makes the scheme practical for very large computations.
\end{document}

